Solution:
Note that
$$
\begin{aligned}
2 \cdot 6 \cdot 10 \cdots (4n-2) &= 2^n \cdot 1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdots (2n-1) \\
&= 2^n \cdot \frac{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdots 2n}{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 6 \cdots 2n} \\
&= \frac{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdots 2n}{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdots n}
\end{aligned}
$$
that is, it is just $\frac{(2n)!}{n!}$. Therefore, since $\frac{(2n)!}{(n!)^2} = \binom{2n}{n}$ is always an integer, the answer is $2005$.

